---
description: No solid black/hard outlines on cards or separators; use elevation
alwaysApply: true
---

# Elevation, not outlines

Do not put solid black, near-black, or high-contrast 1px strokes on cards, list rows, panels, dropdowns, tab strips, or section separators. Hard outlines make the product look boxed-in and complicated.

Use instead:
- White / tinted fill on the page wash
- Purple-tinted `shadow-elevation-*` (or matching CSS shadows)
- Soft inset wells (`surface-inset`, `soft-panel`) for nested regions
- Spacing and background shift for list grouping (`soft-list`), not `divide-y` / `border-b`

Cards (`surface-card` and Access panels): `border: none`, `overflow: visible` so menus can escape. Do not add `overflow-hidden` on a card that hosts a dropdown.

Inputs and ghost/secondary buttons: filled surface + focus/hover glow. Not an outlined box.

Exception: a faint tinted ring is OK for selected/focus state (e.g. `ring-primary/25`), not as the default card chrome.
